# {{ package_name }} — Package Instructions

These instructions supplement the repository root `AGENTS.md` for work under
`src/{{ package_name }}/`.

## Scope

- This is a reusable Django app installed into host projects via `INSTALLED_APPS`.
  Do not add project-only concerns (settings, WSGI/ASGI, deployment) here.
- Keep the public import surface small and stable; it is the package's contract.
{% if use_shinobi %}
- Expose API endpoints as a django-shinobi `Router` in `api.py` for the host to mount;
  do not create a project-owned `NinjaAPI` here.
{% endif %}

## Implementation Invariants

- Ship migrations with the package; add a migration in the same change as a model change.
- Keep the package importable without a configured Django project at import time
  (no settings access at module import).
- Keep the app type-clean (`py.typed` ships); run pyright.

## Validation

- Write or update tests in `tests/` (pytest-django, sqlite) before production code.
- Run `make test`, `make lint`, and `make typecheck`.
- Run `make build` when packaging or the public surface changes.
